Keep the program's files beside the program

LibUltraShip keeps a program's settings file (<name>.cfg.json), its log (logs/<name>.log), the GUI's window layout
(imgui.ini) and the rest in Context::GetAppDirectoryPath. On Linux and Windows that is SHIP_HOME when set, else ".",
the folder the program was started from. Started from another folder, the program then reads and writes a second set
of these files there: it starts with other settings (another key mapping), and its log is not where it was last time.

The fallback is now the folder that holds the program (Context::GetAppBundlePath: /proc/self/exe on Linux, the
module's path on Windows), so one set of files belongs to each build of the program wherever it is started from.
SHIP_HOME still chooses another folder.

diff --git a/src/ship/core/Context.cpp b/src/ship/core/Context.cpp
index ea34621d..b84bbfc6 100644
--- a/src/ship/core/Context.cpp
+++ b/src/ship/core/Context.cpp
@@ -360,7 +360,8 @@ std::string Context::GetAppDirectoryPath(const std::string& appName) {
     }
 #endif
 
-    return ".";
+    // The folder that holds the program, rather than the one it was started from.
+    return GetAppBundlePath();
 }
 
